---
description: PHP / WordPress conventions and the REST-endpoint seam
globs: ["**/*.php"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- WordPress Coding Standards, enforced by phpcs (`phpcs.xml`, ruleset `WordPress`,
  `testVersion 7.4-`): tabs, `snake_case`, WordPress hook naming, PHP 7.4+, lines
  under 120 chars. Autofix only files you touched: `yarn lint:php:fix`.
- Namespaced `TranslateWP\` (PSR-4 from repo root, composer autoload) — no manual
  `require_once` for classes. Guard executable entry points with
  `defined('WPINC')`/`defined('ABSPATH')`; not autoloaded class files. `wp_die()`
  for fatal admin errors, never `die()`/`exit` with user-facing output.
- Avoid custom DB tables — prefer `wp_options`, transients, or custom post types
  (`Entities/CPTs/`). Extend behaviour through WordPress filters/actions; expose a
  filter before changing a preference-driven default.

REST endpoints:
- Register only as plubo-routes `GetEndpoint`/`PostEndpoint` in
  `Functionality/Endpoints/`, wired through `Includes/Loader.php`. Never call
  `register_rest_route` directly.
- Every endpoint takes a `*_permissions_check` capability callback and verifies a
  nonce.
- Sanitize every `$request` param (`sanitize_*`/`esc_*`) before use; escape output;
  `$wpdb->prepare` for dynamic queries.

i18n: wrap user-visible strings (`__`, `esc_html__`, `_x`, `_n`, …) in the
`translate` text domain; translate whole sentences, no HTML inside strings, use
`…`. Config/secrets read only in `Components/RemoteApi.php`. Use `CONTEXT.md`
vocabulary. Verify with `yarn lint:php`.

Full rules: `AGENTS.md`.
